Resolve nested mount points before shortening to a storage root.

TWFunc::GetRootPath() truncates a path to its first component so that
'/data/media/0/x.zip' becomes '/data'. The partition lookups reused it, so a
partition mounted below the first level (e.g. /mnt/vendor/nvdata, which MTK
device trees use for nvdata, nvcfg, protect_f and protect_s) resolved to
'/mnt'. FindPartitionByPath() then failed to see the partition that
ProcessFstab() had just created, so AddRemainingTwrpFlags() added a second
partition for the same mount point (duplicate rows in the Mount list) and
MountByPath()/WipeByPath()/... could not find any partition at all.

Look the exact mount point up first and only fall back to GetRootPath().

